From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:29:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 62/75] rtl: WASI FExpand: do not prefix rooted paths with a
 drive

On WASI FPC_FEXPAND_DRIVES is defined, but DriveSeparator is empty and
paths have no drive letters. For a rooted path FExpand prepends
"S[1] + DriveSeparator" of the base path, i.e. '/', so
ExpandFileName('/a/b') returns '//a/b'. This breaks programs that
compare or look up expanded paths (module resolution, configuration
file discovery).

Only take the drive from the base path when it really starts with a
drive ("X:"); a rooted path is otherwise already complete.
---
 rtl/inc/fexpand.inc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rtl/inc/fexpand.inc b/rtl/inc/fexpand.inc
index 2e9093f6..f15519ba 100644
--- a/rtl/inc/fexpand.inc
+++ b/rtl/inc/fexpand.inc
@@ -389,11 +389,19 @@ begin
                             PathStart := Succ (I);
    {$ENDIF FPC_FEXPAND_DIRSEP_IS_UPDIR}
   {$ELSE FPC_FEXPAND_VOLUMES}
+   {$IFDEF WASI}
+                            { WASI: the base path has a drive only when it
+                              starts with a letter and ':'; otherwise a rooted
+                              path is already complete (no '//' prefix). }
+                            if (Length (S) > 1) and (S [2] = ':') then
+   {$ENDIF WASI}
+                            begin
                             TmpS := S[1] + DriveSeparator;
   {$IF defined(FPC_FEXPAND_SYSUTILS) and not defined(SYSUTILSUNICODE)}
                             SetCodePage(TmpS, DefaultFileSystemCodePage, false);
   {$ENDIF FPC_FEXPAND_SYSUTILS and not SYSUTILSUNICODE}
                             Pa := TmpS + Pa;
+                            end;
   {$ENDIF FPC_FEXPAND_VOLUMES}
                         end;
                 end
